{{also|émulsion|emulsión|Emulsion}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂melǵ-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|émulsion}}, from {{der|en|NL.|ēmulsiō|ēmulsiō, ēmulsiōnis}}, based on {{der|en|la|ēmulgeō||I milk out, extract}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-emulsion.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[stable]] [[suspension]] of small [[droplet]]s of one [[liquid]] in another with which it is [[immiscible]].
#: {{ux|en|Mayonnaise is an '''emulsion''' where egg is used to keep oil and water mixed.}}
# {{lb|en|physical chemistry}} A [[colloid]] in which both [[phase]]s are liquid.
# {{lb|en|photography}} The coating of [[photosensitive]] [[silver]] [[halide]] grains in a thin [[gelatine]] [[layer]] on a [[photographic]] [[film]].

